my co-founder major has a phrase he says  which I love which is that all the  advice in the world sums up to zero  there's very few people who knows  exactly what's right for you and  ultimately it's okay if you're the only  one in the world who sees the value of  what you're building  chipper is a mobile based Financial  platform that is targeted towards people  living in Africa and Out of Africa  offering a whole Suite of financial  products and services from cross-border  payments to investing in  cryptocurrencies and U.S fractional  stocks to issuing Visa debit cards and  also offering a bunch of business to  business solutions  me and my co-founder majored we both  grew up in Africa I was born and raised  in Uganda major was born and raised in  Ghana and we both saw firsthand how  difficult it was for people to send  money from one person to another but  also from one country to another within  Africa and for us that was a clear space  that we thought we could contribute to  so when we met in college it was  something that brought us together in  terms of trying to solve that problem  we've raised over 300 million dollars  today in Venture Capital the company  valued at over 2 billion dollars as of  the last round we have over 400  employees web officers in New York  Nigeria  Uganda Ghana and we're expanding in more  areas as we increase our operational  base  my first inspiration to do anything  entrepreneurial came from my parents  both self-employed my entire life they  worked together both as farmers and in  other Ventures my dad is a computer  Scientist by training so he has an I.T  Farm but there wasn't really a computer  science Industry in Uganda so in many  ways he couldn't explore the the limits  of his own ambition in that sense but he  instilled a great sense of  Entrepreneurship in me watching him and  my mom walk together and for me the idea  of being able to solve a problem every  day was more exciting than anything I  could think of so I knew my entire life  I wanted to do something on my own that  was important that you could build a big  business around  [Music]  we launched in our fast Market in late  2018. in the beginning we thought we  might have some demand for our product  we didn't expect it to be this much we  also didn't expect it to be this  difficult in terms of how many hurdles  you have to jump through to to make  something work the most challenging part  I think has been  not knowing what we don't know you know  you're running too many walls many that  you don't anticipate you're running to  so whatever you think it's going to take  a cost to get something done it usually  takes some costs three times or four  times as much in the very early days  that's in the first one  two years the biggest challenge is just  being able to attract people to invest  and care about what we're doing as a  serious Venture a lot of people on the  surface looked at us is something that  was philanthropic because it dealt with  Africa they didn't see a big opportunity  there they didn't understand the market  and so they didn't really pay us much  mind and it was hard to attract  investment in the company but we've  since we've just been able to solve that  problem and we've been able to show that  there's a great opportunity here and  we've been able to raise quite a bit of  capital to date and that's allowed us to  invest aggressively in things that I  think will help us over the long term  [Music]  ultimately I think the most important  determinant of success is perseverance  more than anything I think if you stick  to what you're trying to do instead of  course you're more likely to succeed  than if you try to do anything else  every time I hear a story is about how  chipper has been a positive impact to  someone in someone's life that's a  reminder to me that uh that story is  important and justifies all the pain  that we've gone through to get the  company to where it's at today  [Music]  thank you
 

